From 2b9c46ed5be99b7d938388f1f0ac183b186eb884 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:18:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/19] dcomp: Implement D3D11-backed desktop composition.

Chromium's DirectComposition path creates a desktop device on its D3D11
device, builds a tree of visuals carrying composition swap chains and
surfaces, and commits it to a target window. Implement enough of
IDCompositionDesktopDevice, IDCompositionVisual2, IDCompositionTarget and
IDCompositionSurface for that.

Commit walks the visual tree of every target and asks DXVK, through its
private composition swap chain interface, to present each swap chain to the
target window. Swap chains that are not opaque get a child host window at
the visual's placement instead, so that they can be layered over the target.
The host window class is registered with the module's own instance.

Visuals, surfaces and targets hold a reference on the device, a target keeps
its root alive and a visual keeps its linked children alive, so nothing is
torn down behind the application's back. Content is unbound from DXVK before
it is released or replaced.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
